        <section class="section">
          <h2 class="section-heading">The short version</h2>
          <article class="prose" style="max-width: 760px; margin-top: 24px;">
            <p>I&rsquo;m Xabier Ariznabarreta. I grew up in Bilbao and now study <strong>AI Engineering</strong> at Universidad Francisco de Vitoria in Madrid. While finishing high school I started building agentic systems on the side. Year and a half later I&rsquo;ve sent several to production: commercial agents integrated with Salesforce, MCP servers with security-review loops, Android field assistants, multilingual institutional tooling.</p>
            <p>The work was useful. It was also a teacher. The bugs were instructive, the customers were patient, and the experience showed me where the bottleneck is &mdash; not in the engineering, but in the science underneath.</p>
            <p>So I&rsquo;m pivoting. I&rsquo;m working on my first empirical paper (an ablation study of agent-harness components), going through <strong>ARENA</strong> in parallel, and using this site as the public notebook for both. Builder in the concrete, learner in the deep.</p>

            <h2>What you&rsquo;ll find here</h2>
            <p>Four kinds of posts:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Technical deep-dives</strong> &mdash; rigorous explanations of LLM concepts, transformer internals, mech interp, eval methodology. Depth before speed.</li>
              <li><strong>Research notes</strong> &mdash; work-in-progress on the harness-ablation paper. Hypotheses, design choices, null findings included.</li>
              <li><strong>Production lessons</strong> &mdash; honest case studies from systems I&rsquo;ve shipped, including the expensive mistakes.</li>
              <li><strong>Meta journey</strong> &mdash; reflections on the builder-to-researcher pivot at 19, ARENA progress, decisions I&rsquo;m reversing, honest self-critique.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </section>

